{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 24, :comments ["<b>All the gold.</b> Scripture testifies to the limited quantity of gold, silver, and copper that went into the work of the Tabernacle — a very small amount compared to the wealth that was in the First Temple, as explained in the book of Kings (I Kings 6:20–35, 7:45–50), and still more so compared to the wealth in the structure built by Herod (Sotah 51a). Yet despite all this, the visible glory of YHWH dwelt more constantly in the Tabernacle of Moses than in the First Temple, and was not seen at all in the Second. By this He demonstrated that neither the quantity of wealth nor the grandeur of the structure is the cause for the indwelling of the Shekhinah among Israel, but rather HaShem desires those who fear Him and their deeds, to dwell among them."], :book :exodus, :voice :sforno, :lang :en, :chapter 38, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T16:28:23.661746557Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}